<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cividale del Friuli</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cividale del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a> is a town in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> as Forum Iulii, from which the region of Friuli takes its name. In 568 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alboin">Alboin</a> left his nephew Gisulf there as the first Lombard duke in Italy. It remained the seat of the Duchy of Friuli, and its Lombard Tempietto is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cividale-del-friuli.jpg" alt="Cividale del Friuli" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ewgohl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cividale_in_panoramic.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
